                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p><strong>Lunch lecture “Optimising your use of the EUR Data Repository”</strong></p>\n<p>Would you like your research to be more visible and impactful? We invite you to a lunch lecture by the EDR Project Lead Nynke de Groot (EUR University Library) on how the EUR Data Repository (EDR) can help you with that.</p>\n<p>The EUR Data Repository an online platform for showcasing your research and making it findable, citable, and reusable. The presentation will guide you through the basic process of publishing your research outputs in the EDR. It will also discuss connecting your EDR account to other tools such as the Open Science Framework, GitHub, and ORCID which allows to automate tracking of your publications.</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
